CUT(1)

NAME
     cut - pick columns out of each line

SYNOPSIS
     cut -f fields [-d separator] [file ...]
     cut -c columns [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
     Keeps part of every line and drops the rest.

     -f fields     keep these fields. Fields are separated by tabs,
                   unless -d names another separator.
     -d c          use the character c as the field separator.
     -c columns    keep these character positions instead.

     A list may be one number (1), several (1,3) or a range (2-4).

EXAMPLES
     cut -f1 /usr/adm/usage.log
     cut -d: -f1 /etc/passwd

SEE ALSO
     sort(1), uniq(1)
